19 and 2020 in characteristics and circumstances for all overdose deaths and for those among Hispanic persons\"}]}],\"data_source_type\":[{\"v\":\"CDC surveillance system\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"SUDORS is a CDC surveillance system containing detailed information on death scene investigations, toxicology, and other risk factors\"}]}],\"data_source_named\":[{\"v\":\"State Unintentional Drug Overdose Reporting System (SUDORS)\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 1\",\"q\":\"Source: Nevada State Unintentional Drug Overdose Reporting System 2019–2020.\"}]}],\"setting\":{\"v\":\"US subnational\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"title\",\"q\":\"Increase in Drug Overdose Deaths Among Hispanic or Latino Persons — Nevada, 2019–2020\"}]},\"vaccine_outcome_type\":null,\"equity\":{\"level\":2,\"level_reason\":\"Hispanic decedents' increase (119.7%) and characteristics are set beside all decedents' (54.5%), with no computed difference or ratio between groups and no population rates, so the contrast is side by side and capped at 2.\",\"level_confidence\":\"medium\",\"level_alternative\":{\"level\":3,\"reason\":\"The headline contrasts a 119.7% increase among Hispanic persons with 54.5% overall and calls for targeted prevention, which could be read as a quantified, interpreted disparity.\"},\"dimensions\":[{\"v\":\"race/ethnicity\",\"role\":\"primary comparison\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"title\",\"q\":\"Increase in Drug Overdose Deaths Among Hispanic or Latino Persons — Nevada, 2019–2020\"},{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Hispanic persons were identified through the SUDORS ethnicity variable\"}]},{\"v\":\"age\",\"role\":\"stratifier\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 1\",\"q\":\"Age group, yrs › <25\"}]},{\"v\":\"sex\",\"role\":\"stratifier\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 1\",\"q\":\"Sex › Male\"}]}],\"determinants_of_health\":{\"v\":null,\"ev\":[]},\"equity_action\":{\"v\":false,\"ev\":[]},\"equity_measurement\":\"Hispanic decedents are compared with all decedents, which include them; there are no population denominators, so only counts, shares and percent changes are compared.\"},\"groupwise\":[{\"across\":[\"age\"],\"n_groups\":5,\"ordered\":true,\"assessment\":\"per-group vs referent only\",\"resolves_to_finer\":true,\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"the highest percentage increases occurred among males (overall = 6.9%; Hispanic persons = 6.2%) and those aged <25 years\"},{\"loc\":\"table 1\",\"q\":\"Age group, yrs › <25\"}]}],\"uncertain_fields\":[\"groupwise\",\"equity.level\"],\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"notes\":\"Percent changes are hand arithmetic. Year-to-year tests are run per table row (age-share changes by year), read as per-category tests across the five age groups. Hispanic deaths are included in the all-deaths group.\",\"view_issues\":\"Text says the highest percentage increases were among males (6.9%), though <25 years rose 77.6%. 'Higher among Hispanic persons' for naloxone rests on no reported test.\"}", "type": "text"}]}